---
import MemoryChart from "../MemoryChart.astro";
---

<span id="blocking-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
  id="blocking-close-title"
  class="anchor-alias"
  aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="built-in-title">
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">the blocker is part of the browser</p>
    <h2 id="built-in-title">Start protected, not set up.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Built around the web, not a browser store.</h3>
      <p>
        Blanc Blocker loads its lists directly in the browser. You do not need
        to find, install, or manage an extension before browsing.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Know the site, not just the count.</h3>
      <p>
        Open the shield to see whether the page uses HTTPS and how many requests
        Blanc blocked. It reports only what the address proves, without turning
        the browser into a security dashboard.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Let a site through when you choose.</h3>
      <p>
        Need a site exception? Use the switch in the shield popover, or type <code
          >/allow-ads</code
        >. Blanc keeps the choice specific to that site instead of making it an
        all-or-nothing setting.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="truth-note-title">
  <p class="section-kicker">good to know</p>
  <h2 id="truth-note-title">Blocking is a strong default, not a guarantee.</h2>
  <p>
    Blanc uses EasyList and EasyPrivacy to reduce ads and known tracking. No
    blocker can promise to remove every advertisement or tracker, and some sites
    may need an exception to work as intended.
  </p>
  <a class="text-link" href="/privacy#browsing-the-web-with-blanc"
    >Read Blanc's network and privacy details <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span
    ></a
  >
</aside>

<section
  class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--report"
  aria-labelledby="missed-ad-title"
>
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">help improve coverage</p><h2 id="missed-ad-title">
      An ad got through? Send a reproducible example.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>A page we can test</h3><p>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/bnfy/blanc/issues/new?template=ad_blocking.yml"
          >Report a missed ad</a
        > with its page URL, Blanc version, operating system, blocker settings, expected
        result and the ad you observed. A screenshot is optional. For examples containing
        private information, email <!--email_off-->
        <a href="mailto:support@blancbrowser.com">support@blancbrowser.com</a
        ><!--/email_off-->.
      </p><p>
        Reports help distinguish filter coverage, a blocker integration defect
        and an ad format the blocker does not support. A report is closed with
        reproduction and verification evidence, or a documented limitation.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<MemoryChart
  headingId="blocking-memory-title"
  kicker="what blocking is worth"
  heading="Blocking saves memory, not just noise."
  intro="Ads and trackers cost real memory to render. With six ad-heavy news sites open, blocking them at the network layer is worth gigabytes."
/>
